  "description": "<p>Given an integer <code>n</code>, return <em><code>true</code> if it is a power of two. Otherwise, return <code>false</code></em>.</p> <p>An integer <code>n</code> is a power of two, if there exists an integer <code>x</code> such that <code>n == 2<sup>x</sup></code>.</p> <p> </p> <p><strong class=\"example\">Example 1:</strong></p> <pre><strong>Input:</strong> n = 1\n<strong>Output:</strong> true\n<strong>Explanation: </strong>2<sup>0</sup> = 1\n</pre> <p><strong class=\"example\">Example 2:</strong></p> <pre><strong>Input:</strong> n = 16\n<strong>Output:</strong> true\n<strong>Explanation: </strong>2<sup>4</sup> = 16\n</pre> <p><strong class=\"example\">Example 3:</strong></p> <pre><strong>Input:</strong> n = 3\n<strong>Output:</strong> false\n</pre> <p> </p> <p><strong>Constraints:</strong></p> <ul> <li><code>-2<sup>31</sup> &lt;= n &lt;= 2<sup>31</sup> - 1</code></li> </ul> <p> </p> <strong>Follow up:</strong> Could you solve it without loops/recursion?",
  "hints": [],
